    <div class="email-body ">
      <p>Howdy, you log is now available in the staging list.  Welcome!

  <a target="_blank" href="https://staging.witness-network.org/log-list-10qps-4klogs.1">https://staging.witness-network.org/log-list-10qps-4klogs.1</a>

-Rasmus

On Fri, Oct 30, 2026 at 09:51:38AM +0000, Александр Артамохов via Participate wrote:</p>
<div class="quoted-switch"><a href="#">...</a></div><blockquote class="blockquote quoted-text"><p>Hello, I would like to request that HISTOR's log be added to the staging witness network, on the 10qps list. vkey histor.modelmarket.dev/log+ad3ca066+AfXpkWqXVW93sChXnhKsNzvGLTFAAredl1jLlEjbr4wU qpd 144 contact alexar76@rambler.ru Origin line: histor.modelmarket.dev/log (equal to the vkey key name). Key type 0x01, Ed25519. Checkpoint: <a target="_blank" href="https://histor.modelmarket.dev/checkpoint">https://histor.modelmarket.dev/checkpoint</a> <a target="_blank" href="https://histor.modelmarket.dev/checkpoint">https://histor.modelmarket.dev/checkpoint</a> Add-checkpoint rate: one request per witness every 10 minutes (144 per day), from a timer on the log's host. The log only grows; consistency proofs are served at <a target="_blank" href="https://histor.modelmarket.dev/api/v1/log/proof/consistency?first=&amp;second=">https://histor.modelmarket.dev/api/v1/log/proof/consistency?first=&second=</a> <a target="_blank" href="https://histor.modelmarket.dev/api/v1/log/proof/consistency?first=&amp;second=">https://histor.modelmarket.dev/api/v1/log/proof/consistency?first=&second=</a> and the witness client handles 409 by resubmitting from the witness's size. What it is: HISTOR is a public, append-only log of the tool definitions that MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers listed in the official MCP registry actually serve. Each observation becomes a signed statement, and the statements are leaves of an RFC 9162 Merkle tree (currently about 1.29 million leaves, growing by a few thousand a day). The format is specified at <a target="_blank" href="https://github.com/alexar76/histor/blob/main/docs/spec/transparency-log.md">https://github.com/alexar76/histor/blob/main/docs/spec/transparency-log.md</a> <a target="_blank" href="https://github.com/alexar76/histor/blob/main/docs/spec/transparency-log.md">https://github.com/alexar76/histor/blob/main/docs/spec/transparency-log.md</a> with